      "id": "dc6cfea3",
      "agent_input": "Hi, I\u2019d like to create a short report from the Q3 sales file that lists only my won deals\u2014D001, D003, D006, and D009 with their amounts. Please help me extract these from data/sales_q3.csv and save them as a new file.",
      "agent_response": {
        "response": "[Awaiting tool approval]\n\n**Policy:** Shell command approval (skills demo)\nAbout to run a shell command in the agent workspace. Approve to continue?\n**Required Tools:** run_command\n```python\nfiles = await list_files(\"./data\")\nprint(files)\n\ncontent = await read_file(\"./data/sales_q3.csv\")\nprint(content)\n\nskill_info = await load_skill(\"OfficeBench\")\nprint(skill_info)\n\nawait run_command(\"uv pip install openpyxl python-docx pdfplumber\")\nimport asyncio\nawait asyncio.sleep(5)\nverify = await run_command('python -c \"import openpyxl; print(\\'ok\\')\"')\nprint(verify)\n\ncontent = await read_file(\"./data/sales_q3.csv\")\nprint(content)\n\nimport re\n\n# Parse the CSV content\nlines = content.strip().split('\\n')\nheader = lines[0]\ntarget_ids = {\"D001\", \"D003\", \"D006\", \"D009\"}\n\n# Filter rows matching the target deal IDs\nwon_deals = [header]\nfor line in lines[1:]:\n    deal_id = line.split(',')[0].strip()\n    if deal_id in target_ids:\n        won_deals.append(line)\n\nreport_content = '\\n'.join(won_deals) + '\\n'\nprint(f\"Found {len(won_deals)-1} won deals:\")\nprint(report_content)\n\nresult = await write_file(\"./output/won_deals_q3.csv\", report_content)\nprint(result)\n\nverification = await read_file(\"./output/won_deals_q3.csv\")\nprint(verification)\n```",
        "status_code": null
      },
